<title>SOUTH KOREA: Daehan seeks 24,500 tonnes U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Daehan seeks 24,500 tonnes U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Daehan Flour Mills Co Ltd on Wednesday invited tenders to buy 24,500 tonnes of U.S. No.1 wheat, traders said.  </p>
<p>Traders said the total amount would be split into four postions -- 11,000 tonnes of western white/soft white, 1,000 tonnes of western white (protein minimum 10 percent), 2,000 tonnes of hard red winter (protein minimum 11.5 percent), and 10,500 tonnes of dark northern spring (protein minimum 14 percent).</p>
<p>Shipment was set for May 1-30 to the western port of Inchon.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
